# Agent efficiency

Inspect only relevant files. Smallest complete change. Changed-file diagnostics,
not suites. No drive-by refactors, todo lists for 1–2 steps, or subagents unless
the search is broad, CI failed, or the user asked.

## Tests

Do not write or run tests unless the user asks, or they ask for a PR. Then
follow `testing.mdc` once. Do not rerun green suites. Do not debug by running
tests that do not exist yet. Do not open a PR until `quality-gate.mdc` pre-PR
steps are green.

## Failed GitHub checks

Do not dump `gh run view --log-failed`. Take the failing job, grep
`FAIL|Error:|Cannot find module|ELIFECYCLE`. Read only the matching hunk.
One red check → one hypothesis → one fix → push. Do not mix lockfile edits,
Docker, and drive-by deletes in the same pass. Do not poll green CI.

If the stack already names a missing module or file, do not open Context7,
library docs, or web search.

## Lockfile / deps

Host Node may be 20; CI is **22.18**. Never regenerate `package-lock.json` with
Windows npm. Use `node:22.18` (Docker). Do not read the lockfile — `npm ls` or
grep a package key. Feature PRs must not mix audit/lockfile churn; split deps.

Keep progress silent except blockers.
